{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1503","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1503","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1503\",\"parent_revision\":\"173914f98347a84b91e7ca1f36d586514bacb828246680c11f0cbbaba193f69b\",\"root_revision\":\"173914f98347a84b91e7ca1f36d586514bacb828246680c11f0cbbaba193f69b\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAll 8 sam_* tools in sam_schema/server.py use synchronous `def` with no `ctx: Context` parameter. Logging goes to `_log = logging.getLogger(__name__)` (server.py line 43) which writes to server stderr only \u2014 MCP clients receive nothing. `sam_create` is the most impacted: it parses YAML, validates tasks, writes a plan file, and makes GitHub API calls for artifact registration (lines 477-478) \u2014 all with zero client visibility. FastMCP `Context` provides `ctx.info()`, `ctx.debug()`, `ctx.request_id`, and `ctx.report_progress()` which send signals back to the calling client over the MCP session.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**VERIFIED** \u2014 No `ctx: Context` parameter on any of the 8 tool functions. Evidence:\\n\\n- `sam_read` (line 112), `sam_state` (line 161), `sam_ready` (line 187), `sam_status` (line 237), `sam_list` (line 302), `sam_create` (line 424), `sam_update` (line 511), `sam_claim` (line 582) \u2014 all are bare `def` with no `ctx` parameter.\\n- Logger declared at line 43 (`_log = logging.getLogger(__name__)`), not line 48 as cited. Minor discrepancy; does not affect validity.\\n- Artifact registration in `sam_create` is at lines 477-478, not 524-525 as cited. Minor discrepancy; the claim that it happens with zero client visibility is correct.\\n- No `@mcp.tool` decorator passes `context=True` or includes a `ctx: Context` injection.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nType: **feature** (missing capability)\\n\\nRoot-Cause Analysis: Initial implementation focused on functional correctness of plan/task operations. FastMCP `Context` injection was not added. No architectural blocker prevents adding it \u2014 FastMCP injects `Context` automatically when a parameter typed `Context` is present in the tool signature.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py:111\u2013621` \u2014 producer (all 8 tools); add `ctx: Context` to each signature\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py` \u2014 consumer (tests); verify they still pass after signature change\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- MCP clients (Claude Code agents, MCP Inspector, other clients) receive no observability during tool execution.\\n- `sam_create` \u2014 the most write-heavy tool (YAML parse \u2192 validate \u2192 file write \u2192 GitHub API) \u2014 gives no feedback if it stalls or partially fails.\\n- No `ctx.request_id` means correlated log tracing across client and server is impossible.\\n- Severity: low (tools function correctly without it) but high value for debugging and long-running plan creation.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nNone \u2014 `Context` is already available via `from fastmcp import FastMCP` (FastMCP is imported at line 31). No additional dependencies required.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] All 8 `sam_*` tool functions accept `ctx: Context` as a final parameter (FastMCP injects it automatically, no callers need updating)\\n- [ ] `sam_create` emits `ctx.info()` at YAML parse, task validation, file write, and artifact registration steps\\n- [ ] `sam_create` calls `ctx.report_progress(step, total)` at each major stage\\n- [ ] `sam_read`, `sam_status`, `sam_ready`, `sam_list`, `sam_state`, `sam_update`, `sam_claim` emit at least `ctx.debug()` on entry with the resolved plan/task address\\n- [ ] Existing tests in `test_server_sam_taskbackend.py` continue to pass (FastMCP test client handles `Context` injection automatically)\\n- [ ] No new tests are required to break; add coverage for `ctx.report_progress` call count in `sam_create` if feasible\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nEstimate: **S**\\nReasoning: Mechanical signature change across 8 tools plus adding structured log/progress calls to `sam_create`. No architectural change. Test suite already covers the tools.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nObserve by inspecting any tool signature:\\n\\n```bash\\ngrep -n \\\"def sam_\\\" plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py\\n```\\n\\nNo tool signature includes `ctx`. Contrast with FastMCP pattern:\\n\\n```python\\nfrom fastmcp import Context\\n\\n@mcp.tool\\ndef sam_create(slug: str, ..., ctx: Context) -> dict:\\n    ctx.info(\\\"Creating plan: %s\\\", slug)\\n    ...\\n    ctx.report_progress(1, 3)\\n    ...\\n```\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want **SAM MCP tools to emit progress, logs, and request correlation via FastMCP Context** so that **MCP clients can observe long-running operations and correlate errors to specific requests**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: FastMCP review of P912 \u2014 .tmp/scratch/reports/fastmcp-review-P912.md\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"87e8e5a57103546a868f355dd54c037a4ec864e7ec056b8b4ec26a72fc119db1\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSdsASg\"}"}